    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50631" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">versōrĭa</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vors-</span></b> ), ae, f.
		verto, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a rope that guides a sail</i>, <i>a sheet</i>
			(Plautin.); hence, trop.: versoriam capere, <i>to turn
				the sail</i>, i. e. <i>tack</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cape vorsoriam, Recipe te ad erum,</span>”
				
					<i>about ship!</i>
				
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Trin. 4, 3, 19</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cape modo vorsoriam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Merc. 5, 2, 34</span></i>
			.</div>
